load @term/seed/code/group
  find group

# The maximal torus: the largest subgroup of a Lie group that is a product of circles, a maximal set of rotations that
# all commute and can be performed independently at once. Its dimension is the rank of the group, the number of
# independent simultaneous spins. The rank of D4, the rotations of the eight-dimensional arena, is four, and that four
# is read as the four dimensions of spacetime. So the maximal torus is where the dimension of spacetime is counted. The
# form carries the underlying group; being a maximal commuting product of circles is the defining condition.
form maximal-torus
  link group, like group
